+# Full study: Arxiv.«2208.14736».zariski_cancellation_problem.variants.dim_two
+
+## Frozen object
+
+The target is the exact `zariski_cancellation_problem.variants.dim_two`
+declaration from the pinned provider revision `2270d31e8dd611521f979de6d86da364930b7669` at
+`FormalConjectures/Arxiv/2208.14736/ZariskiCancellation.lean:57-62`. The provider record is marked `sorryAx`-dependent;
+its source bytes are statement authority only and are not imported as a proof.
+
+The frozen declaration text is:
+
+```lean
+theorem zariski_cancellation_problem.variants.dim_two {k : Type*} [Field k] :
+    IsCancellative k (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k)
+```
+
+The source definition of `IsCancellative k A` quantifies over every finitely
+generated `k`-algebra `B` and asks that an algebra equivalence
+`A[X] ≃ₐ[k] B[X]` descend to `A ≃ₐ[k] B`. At
+`A = MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k`, the target is Zariski cancellation for the
+affine plane over an arbitrary field.
+
+## Human source boundary
+
+Gupta's pinned survey (`arXiv:2208.14736v1`, PDF SHA-256
+`09a4b62495f6f91996f8c69c8585f35613d5e70d3be40aa6fa3079ee22498ddd`)
+states the historical resolution boundary precisely: Fujita, Miyanishi, and
+Sugie proved the characteristic-zero case; Russell proved the result over
+perfect fields of arbitrary characteristic; and Bhatwadekar--Gupta removed
+the perfectness hypothesis. The survey also identifies the algebraic
+characterization of the affine plane used in the original approach.
+
+That survey is a content-addressed historical and mathematical anchor, not a
+formal proof body. None of the cited papers is available here as a reviewed
+Lean provider, and the pinned Mathlib tree contains no formalization of the
+characterization/cancellation chain. Consequently the human sources justify
+the theorem's mathematical status but cannot be promoted to `M0-P` or used to
+erase the typed machine cut below.
+
+## Resolution frontier
+
+The exact definition, independent universe replay, and both definitional
+transports are kernel-checked. The remaining root is the substantive
+affine-plane cancellation argument; no theorem with this conclusion exists
+in the pinned local Mathlib tree, and the provider body cannot close it.
+
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-00:BEGIN -->
+### PU-00 — exact source statement
+
+`Statement.lean` replays `IsCancellative` with the original binder order and
+defines `FrozenStatement` as
+`IsCancellative k (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k)`. `Target` is definitionally equal
+to that proposition, including the independent universe of `B`.
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-00:END -->
+
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-01:BEGIN -->
+### PU-01 — cancellation obligation expansion
+
+After unfolding the definition, the root obligation is: for arbitrary
+`B : Type v` with `[CommRing B]`, `[Algebra k B]`, and
+`[Algebra.FiniteType k B]`, turn
+`Nonempty ((MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k)[X] ≃ₐ[k] B[X])` into
+`Nonempty (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k ≃ₐ[k] B)`.
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-01:END -->
+
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-02:BEGIN -->
+### PU-02 — canonical polynomial equivalence
+
+`polynomial_self_equivalence` supplies the identity element of
+`Nonempty (A[X] ≃ₐ[k] A[X])`, where
+`A = MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k`. It checks the polynomial-extension input shape
+and does not assert cancellation for an arbitrary `B`.
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-02:END -->
+
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-03:BEGIN -->
+### PU-03 — conditional specialization
+
+`cancellation_specialization` is the exact local consequence of an assumed
+`FrozenStatement`: it exposes the universal `B` branch and forwards a given
+polynomial-extension equivalence to the desired equivalence.  This is a
+diagnostic transport, not a proof of the assumption.
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-03:END -->
+
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-04:BEGIN -->
+### PU-04 — missing mathematical root
+
+The missing declaration must prove `FrozenStatement k` for every field `k`.
+That is precisely the affine-plane Zariski cancellation result. Neither
+the polynomial API nor finite-type infrastructure in the pinned checkout
+provides this implication.
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-04:END -->
+
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-05:BEGIN -->
+### PU-05 — trust boundary
+
+The provider theorem is intentionally excluded because its recorded body uses
+`sorryAx`.  No claim-specific axiom, opaque declaration, unsafe declaration,
+or bodyless oracle is introduced locally.  Ordinary transitive Mathlib
+foundations observed by the probes are disclosed in the machine closure.
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-05:END -->
+
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-06:BEGIN -->
+### PU-06 — composition frontier
+
+A future exact root would compose PU-01 through PU-05 into the theorem
+declaration and then allow `machine_complete` to become true.  The current
+worker can only compose the completed statement/transport diagnostics, so the
+root remains an explicit typed cut.
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-06:END -->
+
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-ROOT-OPEN:BEGIN -->
+### PU-ROOT-OPEN — provisional handoff
+
+The exact trust-zero theorem is not claimed.  This package is a self-tested
+nonacceptance handoff waiting for independent Master review and a future
+replacement proof of the frozen proposition.
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-ROOT-OPEN:END -->
+
+## Conclusion
+
+Identity exactness, statement transport, frontier-anchor reconstruction, and
+cold replay are closed.  `machine_complete`, `readable_complete`, and
+`theorem_complete` remain false: the cancellation root is open, so there is no
+synthesized exact proof to reconstruct or submit to identity-distinct review.
